#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""OptMem: permanent, local, append-first memory for AI agents.

Usage:
  {memo} [--global] <command> [arguments]

Connect and inspect:
  {memo} init                    create global memory and print instructions
  {memo} setup [--create|--no-create] [FILE ...]
                                 add CLI guidance to existing agent files
  {memo} scope                   show automatic project and store selection
  {memo} doctor [--deep]         diagnose setup; optionally verify full stores
  {memo} wake                    read global then project memory
  {memo} wake <part> [T]         continue a paginated project-memory snapshot

Remember and retrieve:
  {memo} note "<one line>"       save one durable project memory
  {memo} show <id>               show one raw memory and later references
  {memo} amend <id> "<one line>" append a corrected replacement
  {memo} retract <id> "<reason>" mark a memory no longer authoritative
  {memo} recall [options] <query>
                                 exact, fuzzy, or optional semantic recall
  {memo} zoom [--depth N] <range>
                                 open one or more summary-tree levels

Maintain:
  {memo} nap [id "..."|--batch N|--apply FILE]
                                 complete one or more compressions
  {memo} resummarize <lo>-<hi>   discard a bad summary; nap rebuilds it
  {memo} redact <id> --force     permanently remove one sensitive payload
  {memo} config [NAME=N]         inspect or change this store's sizes
  {memo} export [--with-ids] [file]
                                 write a portable history
  {memo} import [--dry-run] <file>
                                 restore into an empty store

Optional integrations and installation:
  {memo} qmd [help]              explain or manage optional semantic recall
  {memo} completion <shell>      print bash, zsh, fish, or powershell setup
  {memo} version                 print the installed OptMem version
  {memo} upgrade                 download and validate the latest release
  {memo} uninstall               remove the tool; preserve every memory

Scope precedence:
  MEMORY_DIR pins one explicit store. Otherwise --global selects the memory
  that follows you everywhere. Project commands automatically select a hosted
  Git remote (origin, tracked, or sole); OPTMEM_REMOTE chooses when needed.
  Without one, first memory use creates a move-stable local project marker.

Examples:
  {memo} setup                   teach existing AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md to use memo
  {memo} setup --create          also create either file when missing
  {memo} scope                   preview selection without creating a store
  {memo} note "Retries use capped exponential backoff."
  {memo} --global note "The user prefers PowerShell examples."

Run `{memo} scope` when project selection is unclear; run `{memo} doctor` for
installation or store diagnostics.
See github.com/doeixd/OptMem.
"""

